{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731177Z","id":"d98ab4255e278e6fbb4b1da311ff2e95afa031ccc93e29b5fc93b81214058577","body":{"detail":"A tab hidden for HIDDEN_MS (30 s) releases its topics and fetches its state again when it shows; the shared connection has no per-tab resume point.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":319},"end":{"line":338},"content_hash":"50c522e84cb5cdc1713ecbc3f861987420515d73d6fa24c51e8100ef15d8744e"},"suggested_fix":"Per-topic rings in the worker would let a briefly hidden tab replay instead.","summary":"A hidden tab's catch-up is a refetch","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731211Z","id":"55c90b79a7e526231bc7e5ebdf5e0ac62f9a4eec00f9122f4bbf705541e6f834","body":{"detail":"A tab counts its hub gone after DEAD_MS (35 s) without a ping, or at once where the browser fires close on the worker's port. A worker that lives but hangs is not restarted, since a new SharedWorker of the same name reaches the same instance. Leader tabs are not pinged at all: a hidden leader's timers are throttled and its followers would replace it needlessly; a leader hidden for 30 s leaves, so a frozen tab does not hold the connection for long.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":440},"end":{"line":443},"content_hash":"3643dd1ee71089c5de9eefb664e36a0c9b7381f7a039d5bd1209b1a37d43fcdf"},"summary":"The shared worker is checked only by its pings; a hung worker is not restarted","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:26:52.183528Z","id":"af99e0847d6ce2acbeb8dc02c4fb0ecccc1422f8ce16b5f5205a33dc2489b39e","body":{"detail":"drop() aborts the current connection. When that connection is a GET /api/stream whose response has not reached the page yet, Chrome keeps the socket to drain the response for reuse (about 5 s; the SSE body never ends) and only then closes it, so the daemon counts the stream attached meanwhile (`open` and `levels` in GET /api/_test/stream/open). web/e2e/streams.spec.ts saw two admin streams for about 5 s this way when one rename caused several reopens. The hub now reopens once per caller change, so this remains only when a reopen lands while a connect is in flight. The daemon detaches a closed client within a millisecond; the delay is the browser's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":461},"end":{"line":467},"content_hash":"50f43433859ae4b4960306f84d9917ae901ccd99c2692329e7e275099aa83ca7"},"summary":"A stream request aborted before it answers stays open on the daemon for up to 5 s","tags":["risk","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:26:52.183696Z","id":"39039ebd109e36a9ab6fa0a5b16c7fbc7afba8fa60ff45ae6e1bb7110fbd04b0","body":{"detail":"After getToken() fails, ownerBrowser() retries with its own fetch of /api/token. When that succeeds the browser holds the events cookie, but api.ts's tokenPromise stays unset and its onToken listeners do not run, so the next getToken() fetches the token again, and the page's stream is reopened as the owner's only when the hub's next subscription on the old stream is refused (stream-hub.ts, unknown_stream) or a later getToken() succeeds. web/e2e/streams.spec.ts (the late-token test) shows the stream still reopening once.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":16},"end":{"line":19},"content_hash":"59b34f86a2eaf058ac291d8fa806118099047e4ca5716284f58f1e542cfb2ea4"},"suggested_fix":"Retry through getToken() (after its memo is dropped) so a success sets the memo and runs the onToken listeners.","summary":"ownerBrowser's own token retry leaves getToken's memo failed","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:35:49.946752Z","id":"8525f268fb8a05164766a18851d809e67ab80bd9ab2ce4b3200b0d7281681647","body":{"detail":"drop() aborts the current connection. When that connection is a GET /api/stream whose response has not reached the page yet, Chrome keeps the socket to drain the response for reuse (about 5 s; the SSE body never ends) and only then closes it, so the daemon counts the stream as attached meanwhile (`open` and `levels` in GET /api/_test/stream/open), holding a second stream for the browser. The hub reopens at most once per caller change (the `reconnect` case compares the asked caller with the one the stream's `ready` named), so this happens when a reopen, a reconnect after a refused subscription, or a failure's retry lands while a connect is in flight. The daemon detaches a closed client within a millisecond; the delay is the browser's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":461},"end":{"line":467},"content_hash":"50f43433859ae4b4960306f84d9917ae901ccd99c2692329e7e275099aa83ca7"},"suggested_fix":"Let an in-flight connect reach its `ready` before acting on a reconnect or a refused subscription (decide then, as an ask made while no stream is up already is), so the hub never aborts a stream request that has not answered.","summary":"A stream request aborted before it answers stays open on the daemon for up to 5 s","supersedes":"af99e0847d6ce2acbeb8dc02c4fb0ecccc1422f8ce16b5f5205a33dc2489b39e","tags":["risk","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:38:28.460351Z","id":"0239b9e01e340c099e2641be35f6583631bb99281339a8f3de905ef92a9407ef","body":{"detail":"A tab hidden for HIDDEN_MS (30 s) releases its topics and fetches its state again when it shows; the shared connection has no per-tab resume point.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":323},"end":{"line":342},"content_hash":"50c522e84cb5cdc1713ecbc3f861987420515d73d6fa24c51e8100ef15d8744e"},"suggested_fix":"Per-topic rings in the worker would let a briefly hidden tab replay instead.","summary":"A hidden tab's catch-up is a refetch","supersedes":"d98ab4255e278e6fbb4b1da311ff2e95afa031ccc93e29b5fc93b81214058577","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:38:28.460429Z","id":"87de9a6414227d430f6a7a7d5c5361145e613d37bac16d2064315c645579a079","body":{"detail":"A tab counts its hub gone after DEAD_MS (35 s) without a ping, or at once where the browser fires close on the worker's port. A worker that lives but hangs is not restarted, since a new SharedWorker of the same name reaches the same instance. Leader tabs are not pinged at all: a hidden leader's timers are throttled and its followers would replace it needlessly; a leader hidden for 30 s leaves, so a frozen tab does not hold the connection for long.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":444},"end":{"line":447},"content_hash":"3643dd1ee71089c5de9eefb664e36a0c9b7381f7a039d5bd1209b1a37d43fcdf"},"summary":"The shared worker is checked only by its pings; a hung worker is not restarted","supersedes":"55c90b79a7e526231bc7e5ebdf5e0ac62f9a4eec00f9122f4bbf705541e6f834","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/waiting.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:46:09.795109Z","id":"b68a78ba03e7b2b67859cab95300df5a891e882c2852b57fb3b2752d4a23fce3","body":{"detail":"The daemon now reports state withheld with an approver name (crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs state_of) for a comment held from its agent until the agent's person approves its author; waitingLabel has no case for it, so the thread shows no waiting indicator. Spec §10 wants 'waiting for Sam's approval'. clax comments prints it (crates/clax-cli/src/commands/comments.rs delivery).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":34},"end":{"line":34},"content_hash":"94752ffd9323a0e85d941ed8b7de2099267ddbfee318f8338c4977428961c9be"},"summary":"The shell shows no delivery label for feedback_state withheld","tags":["people","ui","spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:04:39.286782Z","id":"a389fe86a5794375e200f440b6b0cc3f2f7d01702febcd91a16de7706d6b119a","body":{"detail":"drop() aborts the current connection. When that connection is a GET /api/stream whose response has not reached the page yet, Chrome keeps the socket to drain the response for reuse (about 5 s; the SSE body never ends) and only then closes it, so the daemon counts the stream as attached meanwhile (`open` and `levels` in GET /api/_test/stream/open), holding a second stream for the browser. The hub reopens at most once per caller change (the `reconnect` case compares the asked caller with the one the stream's `ready` named), so this happens when a reopen, a reconnect after a refused subscription, or a failure's retry lands while a connect is in flight. The daemon detaches a closed client within a millisecond; the delay is the browser's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":477},"end":{"line":483},"content_hash":"50f43433859ae4b4960306f84d9917ae901ccd99c2692329e7e275099aa83ca7"},"suggested_fix":"Let an in-flight connect reach its `ready` before acting on a reconnect or a refused subscription (decide then, as an ask made while no stream is up already is), so the hub never aborts a stream request that has not answered.","summary":"A stream request aborted before it answers stays open on the daemon for up to 5 s","supersedes":"8525f268fb8a05164766a18851d809e67ab80bd9ab2ce4b3200b0d7281681647","tags":["risk","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:04:39.288387Z","id":"d8cce851555f951af6ccf1ae3b9dfe38ebb76efe1340bada4e9bc10a16ca795e","body":{"detail":"A tab hidden for HIDDEN_MS (30 s) releases its topics and fetches its state again when it shows; the shared connection has no per-tab resume point.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":330},"end":{"line":349},"content_hash":"50c522e84cb5cdc1713ecbc3f861987420515d73d6fa24c51e8100ef15d8744e"},"suggested_fix":"Per-topic rings in the worker would let a briefly hidden tab replay instead.","summary":"A hidden tab's catch-up is a refetch","supersedes":"0239b9e01e340c099e2641be35f6583631bb99281339a8f3de905ef92a9407ef","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:04:39.290026Z","id":"932a69a375afa3ab35f876ff67c6201fde3ec7fd4e715604f4bc917459b6d3df","body":{"detail":"A tab counts its hub gone after DEAD_MS (35 s) without a ping, or at once where the browser fires close on the worker's port. A worker that lives but hangs is not restarted, since a new SharedWorker of the same name reaches the same instance. Leader tabs are not pinged at all: a hidden leader's timers are throttled and its followers would replace it needlessly; a leader hidden for 30 s leaves, so a frozen tab does not hold the connection for long.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":451},"end":{"line":454},"content_hash":"3643dd1ee71089c5de9eefb664e36a0c9b7381f7a039d5bd1209b1a37d43fcdf"},"summary":"The shared worker is checked only by its pings; a hung worker is not restarted","supersedes":"87de9a6414227d430f6a7a7d5c5361145e613d37bac16d2064315c645579a079","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:19:06.766550Z","id":"71fb8686842d19e8c5d54164b3fe1a79e76c68a7bcf5a8bb8a9eed70b683ad7b","body":{"detail":"ownerBrowser() and getToken() ask GET /api/token, which a hosted daemon answers 404 (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs gate). The owner's session is Caller::Owner { browser: true } server-side, but routes taking RequireToken and the shell's token-gated controls stay unavailable. PeopleLink asks /api/hosted/me instead; nothing else does. The gallery header also still reads 'local artifacts'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":12},"content_hash":"ee86ee0c2175c338a5f64f0cf9a302155d98f2bfbc115f4118d64df71edf3701"},"suggested_fix":"Let the shell learn ownership from GET /api/hosted/me in hosted mode and send owner writes without the token where the daemon accepts the owner's browser.","summary":"A hosted owner's browser is never served the token, so the shell's owner surfaces that ask for it are off: the inbox and questions, rename, pin and delete","tags":["hosted","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:55:24.316274Z","id":"cb854195b3ab7ce6015b271925722d2d4f55f89ceafa52c941449b23bb6aa70a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d44e6509","summary":"Fixed: GET /api/token hands a hosted owner's session its shell token (cxo_, an HMAC of the session cookie under a key made from the daemon token; crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs shell_token, token_for), and the gate takes it beside that cookie (and the public Origin for a change) as the daemon token, in Authorization or a WebSocket's token parameter; anyone else gets 403 not_owner, so ownerBrowser() resolves. The gallery bar names the site. Evidence: api_hosted::the_owners_browser_holds_a_shell_token_that_stands_for_the_daemon_token passes (questions, inbox, people, rename, pin, delete; refused without the cookie, beside another browser's, without Origin, after sign out); web/e2e/hosted.spec.ts shows the bar 'localhost:<port> · seen as Ada', Pin and Inbox, and pins a page.","supersedes":"71fb8686842d19e8c5d54164b3fe1a79e76c68a7bcf5a8bb8a9eed70b683ad7b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.162628Z","id":"50fbae8dc711f064037bc747aba83a54ee2a563dda7da6130d8f8ef2aed8dcad","body":{"detail":"After getToken() fails, ownerBrowser() retries with its own fetch of /api/token. When that succeeds the browser holds the events cookie, but api.ts's tokenPromise stays unset and its onToken listeners do not run, so the next getToken() fetches the token again, and the page's stream is reopened as the owner's only when the hub's next subscription on the old stream is refused (stream-hub.ts, unknown_stream) or a later getToken() succeeds. web/e2e/streams.spec.ts (the late-token test) shows the stream still reopening once.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":17},"end":{"line":20},"content_hash":"59b34f86a2eaf058ac291d8fa806118099047e4ca5716284f58f1e542cfb2ea4"},"suggested_fix":"Retry through getToken() (after its memo is dropped) so a success sets the memo and runs the onToken listeners.","summary":"ownerBrowser's own token retry leaves getToken's memo failed","supersedes":"39039ebd109e36a9ab6fa0a5b16c7fbc7afba8fa60ff45ae6e1bb7110fbd04b0","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:08.819479Z","id":"5870069c462f45753a3e950360e0868360aa8c04031b5c74a3593ea7d2478bcb","body":{"detail":"The hub learns that the server carries /api/stream over a WebSocket only from a 426 to the plain request, and remembers it for its own life: once per shared worker, but once per page load where the hub runs in the tab (no SharedWorker). The daemon is unaffected. A server that advertised the transport (in the /a/ bootstrap, or a header on a response the shell already makes) would save the round trip on the time-to-usable path.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":324},"end":{"line":328},"content_hash":"e461307789815f4359eb9af3636cda0d5096499a69ff787f40b9ab7f66444374"},"summary":"On a Worker each new stream hub pays one 426 round trip before it opens the WebSocket","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:18:39.905351Z","id":"e604b4be66fabd7e5bc699b25d1e319d606f305badbf0c33b7c9a9d04c740b3c","body":{"detail":"drop() aborts the current connection. When that connection is a GET /api/stream whose response has not reached the page yet, Chrome keeps the socket to drain the response for reuse (about 5 s; the SSE body never ends) and only then closes it, so the daemon counts the stream as attached meanwhile (`open` and `levels` in GET /api/_test/stream/open), holding a second stream for the browser. The hub reopens at most once per caller change (the `reconnect` case compares the asked caller with the one the stream's `ready` named), so this happens when a reopen, a reconnect after a refused subscription, or a failure's retry lands while a connect is in flight. The daemon detaches a closed client within a millisecond; the delay is the browser's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":529},"end":{"line":535},"content_hash":"50f43433859ae4b4960306f84d9917ae901ccd99c2692329e7e275099aa83ca7"},"suggested_fix":"Let an in-flight connect reach its `ready` before acting on a reconnect or a refused subscription (decide then, as an ask made while no stream is up already is), so the hub never aborts a stream request that has not answered.","summary":"A stream request aborted before it answers stays open on the daemon for up to 5 s","supersedes":"a389fe86a5794375e200f440b6b0cc3f2f7d01702febcd91a16de7706d6b119a","tags":["risk","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:46:43.168948Z","id":"5f5bc57859f2b885409663b911f557d29461631d62739169562fb16a9db8952d","body":{"detail":"After getToken() fails, ownerBrowser() retries with its own fetch of /api/token. When that succeeds the browser holds the events cookie, but api.ts's tokenPromise stays unset and its onToken listeners do not run, so the next getToken() fetches the token again, and the page's stream is reopened as the owner's only when the hub's next subscription on the old stream is refused (stream-hub.ts, unknown_stream) or a later getToken() succeeds. web/e2e/streams.spec.ts (the late-token test) shows the stream still reopening once.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":14},"content_hash":"3583aab0722c57192d9777c50e3b423a5cb5f506f0d69f5340e6a13a39ff815d"},"suggested_fix":"Retry through getToken() (after its memo is dropped) so a success sets the memo and runs the onToken listeners.","summary":"ownerBrowser's own token retry leaves getToken's memo failed","supersedes":"39039ebd109e36a9ab6fa0a5b16c7fbc7afba8fa60ff45ae6e1bb7110fbd04b0","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:46:43.169976Z","id":"731e8dc09a348b80609c99df62d4b1f0864b765b3a0e6eaf5a62440e9a50a493","body":{"detail":"inboxBrowser asks GET /api/inbox?limit=1 after the token is refused, so every page a LAN viewer opens makes one refused request (web/e2e/questions.spec.ts counts it). The gallery already fetches /api/viewers/me, whose viewer carries `person` for a connected person, so it could decide without the extra request; the inbox route answering is the authority on who has an inbox (a revoked person, a narrowed grant), which is why it is asked.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":22},"end":{"line":24},"content_hash":"1c00202836a1793c48a45e75bb5b9ea9a31c6d3a053fadc6a0cad12baf13b1b5"},"summary":"Know a connected person's browser from GET /api/viewers/me (its person flag) instead of a look at /api/inbox","tags":["revisit:LAN viewers' page loads become latency-sensitive, or /api/viewers/me gains an inbox flag","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:48:04.741737Z","id":"27fc3c286225e165c7502d1475ea97fdb0a2db3ccd328f36759f36c872590399","body":{"detail":"On a scratch daemon a LAN viewer made exactly one refused GET /api/inbox?limit=1 per page (/inbox, /, /a/<id>), each logging a 'Failed to load resource: 403' console error beside the existing /api/token ones; nothing of the inbox rendered or leaked. For a connected person the look is a sequential round trip after the /api/token 403 and before the q chunk loads. web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte:97 already fetches GET /api/viewers/me on every page, and its `person`/`person_revoked_at` fields (web/shell/src/people/PeopleLink.svelte:5) answer the same question with no extra request; the artifact view also knows its viewer before artifact-questions.ts runs. Recommendation: gate on the viewer's person flag, keeping /api/inbox's 403 as the authority when the feeds start.","kind":"comment","references":"731e8dc09a348b80609c99df62d4b1f0864b765b3a0e6eaf5a62440e9a50a493","summary":"Measured cost of the /api/inbox look, and why /api/viewers/me looks better","tags":["review","task:21","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:16:17.637527Z","id":"a9690820535f9d2d5c60dff24ad9b6e66d928e36ee3ef014608a3fa47676d2cf","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a5019f38","span":{"start":{"line":22},"end":{"line":24},"content_hash":"9c970c33d9b46f3a88558e76a513e06786ad91e220ff45bdb65f608847714d05"},"summary":"Taken: inboxBrowser now reads the person flag of the page's own GET /api/viewers/me (the gallery's lookup, the artifact view's seeded viewer), else the owner's token; the inbox routes stay the authority when the feeds start. Evidence: e2e/questions.spec.ts, reverted to expect no /api/inbox or /api/questions request from a LAN viewer, passes; in Chromium a plain LAN viewer on /, /inbox and /a/<id> made none, and Ivy's and Jo's browsers made no /api/inbox?limit=1 look.","supersedes":"731e8dc09a348b80609c99df62d4b1f0864b765b3a0e6eaf5a62440e9a50a493","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"43f48499256305c81642d0decec018ccd2d5734c316d1e9ac38c6ab8d1fdc9a0","body":{"detail":"After getToken() fails, ownerBrowser() retries with its own fetch of /api/token. When that succeeds the browser holds the events cookie, but api.ts's tokenPromise stays unset and its onToken listeners do not run, so the next getToken() fetches the token again, and the page's stream is reopened as the owner's only when the hub's next subscription on the old stream is refused (stream-hub.ts, unknown_stream) or a later getToken() succeeds. web/e2e/streams.spec.ts (the late-token test) shows the stream still reopening once.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":15},"content_hash":"3583aab0722c57192d9777c50e3b423a5cb5f506f0d69f5340e6a13a39ff815d"},"suggested_fix":"Retry through getToken() (after its memo is dropped) so a success sets the memo and runs the onToken listeners.","summary":"ownerBrowser's own token retry leaves getToken's memo failed","supersedes":"5f5bc57859f2b885409663b911f557d29461631d62739169562fb16a9db8952d","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"0de6d056a59b5f7f7b32fc7cf91489ac31c28b777c80bf66c6323de42479a24c","body":{"detail":"The hub learns that the server carries /api/stream over a WebSocket only from a 426 to the plain request, and remembers it for its own life: once per shared worker, but once per page load where the hub runs in the tab (no SharedWorker). The daemon is unaffected. A server that advertised the transport (in the /a/ bootstrap, or a header on a response the shell already makes) would save the round trip on the time-to-usable path.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":342},"end":{"line":346},"content_hash":"e461307789815f4359eb9af3636cda0d5096499a69ff787f40b9ab7f66444374"},"summary":"On a Worker each new stream hub pays one 426 round trip before it opens the WebSocket","supersedes":"5870069c462f45753a3e950360e0868360aa8c04031b5c74a3593ea7d2478bcb","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"f7af5d6e1ba912cfadc116fa2e4533c0f7961d5edba9479cab37d1dd306ab6d8","body":{"detail":"drop() aborts the current connection. When that connection is a GET /api/stream whose response has not reached the page yet, Chrome keeps the socket to drain the response for reuse (about 5 s; the SSE body never ends) and only then closes it, so the daemon counts the stream as attached meanwhile (`open` and `levels` in GET /api/_test/stream/open), holding a second stream for the browser. The hub reopens at most once per caller change (the `reconnect` case compares the asked caller with the one the stream's `ready` named), so this happens when a reopen, a reconnect after a refused subscription, or a failure's retry lands while a connect is in flight. The daemon detaches a closed client within a millisecond; the delay is the browser's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":547},"end":{"line":553},"content_hash":"50f43433859ae4b4960306f84d9917ae901ccd99c2692329e7e275099aa83ca7"},"suggested_fix":"Let an in-flight connect reach its `ready` before acting on a reconnect or a refused subscription (decide then, as an ask made while no stream is up already is), so the hub never aborts a stream request that has not answered.","summary":"A stream request aborted before it answers stays open on the daemon for up to 5 s","supersedes":"e604b4be66fabd7e5bc699b25d1e319d606f305badbf0c33b7c9a9d04c740b3c","tags":["risk","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:12.224889Z","id":"7b5e30e3d8813988b144e1d294a7d0b33cc5bec04aba1314c219a3df56ab8907","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"50fbae8dc711f064037bc747aba83a54ee2a563dda7da6130d8f8ef2aed8dcad","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: the same record as 5f5bc57859f2b885409663b911f557d29461631d62739169562fb16a9db8952d (kept), re-anchored on a parallel branch. Proposed close: reason:duplicate.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/waiting.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:23.336895Z","id":"ecad42f2c2c91864e3508cc7d720dc3bb984777ece85fc34b395af113c311017","body":{"detail":"The daemon now reports state withheld with an approver name (crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs state_of) for a comment held from its agent until the agent's person approves its author; waitingLabel has no case for it, so the thread shows no waiting indicator. Spec §10 wants 'waiting for Sam's approval'. clax comments prints it (crates/clax-cli/src/commands/comments.rs delivery).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":35},"end":{"line":35},"content_hash":"94752ffd9323a0e85d941ed8b7de2099267ddbfee318f8338c4977428961c9be"},"summary":"The shell shows no delivery label for feedback_state withheld","supersedes":"b68a78ba03e7b2b67859cab95300df5a891e882c2852b57fb3b2752d4a23fce3","tags":["people","ui","spec:10","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/gallery.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:45:12.360131Z","id":"2147868f93039f2b025258026bd261e1fd75b93901a090a23e8ada5e7e2e0821","body":{"detail":"Failure: scripts/quality_gates.sh's web unit gate failed on this test with TypeError: from_html is not a function at shell/src/ui/GalleryCard.svelte:11, mounting Gallery after the test's own vi.resetModules() (line 451). A full ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run in web/ failed the same way once and passed once; the file alone passed three times; //web:unit under Bazel passed. A Svelte module evaluated half-way across a module reset is the likely cause; not confirmed. The test also waits 50 ms on the clock (line 457).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":444},"end":{"line":459},"content_hash":"12584fda52619295f7f1a8fe7673a8e3d8e3096f2985f220be7a30d17d1ffb5d"},"summary":"'shows People in the header to the owner and to a connected person, and not to a LAN viewer' fails now and then in a full vitest run: from_html is not a function","tags":["tests","flaky","web","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/waiting.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:02:35.345810Z","id":"6b3301dd44a48b7f9cbc91e047927896bf18750a0f9f13932d0295be2bd60988","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:323 maps a sent thread on an `app` session to Tier::Wait, so feedback_state is {state: \"sent\", tier: \"wait\"} until the app's poll takes it. The comment at lines 3-8 says the daemon never emits `sent` with `wait`, and the label at line 13 says \"waiting on its wait_for_feedback loop\", an MCP tool the app's agent does not have (it long-polls GET /api/sessions/<sid>/feedback?tier=wait).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3},"end":{"line":16},"content_hash":"dcd8af521919b3038e22fe84593dff81b0b40a4d78661b533af3babc8e233d52"},"suggested_fix":"Update the comment to say `sent`/`wait` is the app session's state, and word the `wait` label so it fits both an MCP wait_for_feedback call and the app's feedback poll (e.g. \"its feedback poll\").","summary":"Waiting labels: the comment says `sent` never names `wait`, which an app session now does","tags":["review","flutter-app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/waiting.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:05:51.886249Z","id":"138449af9f4ba084253338f29939a8a895e96cd55fdbbb9e6dd0f2d68c24fc92","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:660fdc49","summary":"The comment at web/shell/src/waiting.ts:3-9 now says `sent` names `wait` only for the Clax app's agent; the wait labels read \"its next feedback poll\" and \"its feedback poll\", naming no MCP tool. waiting.test.ts asserts the sent/wait label; `npx vitest run shell` (in web/): 85 files, 748 tests passed; `npm run typecheck`: 0 errors, 0 warnings.","supersedes":"6b3301dd44a48b7f9cbc91e047927896bf18750a0f9f13932d0295be2bd60988","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
